\section{Columns of \code{records}}{
The first two columns say which input each row came from - \code{source_index} is 1-based in R, so it indexes \code{files} directly - and rows are grouped by input, in input order, whatever \code{threads} is.
\describe{
\item{\code{source_index}}{int; never \code{NA}. 0-based input position.}
\item{\code{source_path}}{string; never \code{NA}. Absolute path.}
\item{\code{role}}{string; never \code{NA}. factor_value | sample_characteristic | biological_replicate: which check read this column.}
\item{\code{column_name}}{string; never \code{NA}. The column as the header spells it.}
\item{\code{rows}}{int; in \strong{rows}; never \code{NA}. Rows, counted once per row per column NAME (a repeated column does not inflate it).}
\item{\code{filled}}{int; in \strong{rows}; never \code{NA}. Rows with a real answer in at least one of the column's cells.}
\item{\code{absent}}{int; in \strong{rows}; never \code{NA}. Rows that are empty or a reserved word (any case): rows - filled.}
\item{\code{distinct_values}}{int; in \strong{values}; never \code{NA}. Different real answers, compared case-insensitively after trimming.}
\item{\code{fill_rate}}{float; in \strong{fraction (0-1)}; never \code{NA}. filled / rows; 0 when rows is 0. May cross as an integer 0 or 1.}
}
